---
import '../styles/global.css';
import { nav } from '../layouts';
const technologies = ['Python','TDD','BDD','CI/CD','IaC','Kafka','RabbitMQ'];
const optionalTechnologies = ['AWS','Kubernetes','Terraform','Databricks','Airflow','Kubeflow'];
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f5f1" />
    <title>Task 2 | Make something better</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <div class="shell header-inner">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/prima-employer-brand-takehome/">PRIMA</a>
        <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
          {nav.map((item) => <a href={`/prima-employer-brand-takehome${item.href}`} aria-current={item.href === '/task-2/' ? 'page' : undefined}>{item.label}</a>)}
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="task-hero">
        <div class="shell task-head">
          <div class="task-number"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Make something better</span></div>
          <h1>From job description to candidate decision tool.</h1>
          <p class="lead">I selected a real Prima vacancy and redesigned the mobile experience around the information a candidate needs first.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="shell grid two">
          <article class="surface card">
            <div class="eyebrow">Asset selected</div>
            <h2 style="margin-top:10px">Senior Python Software Engineer</h2>
            <p style="margin-top:8px">Prima Careers · Milan · Engineering</p>
            <div class="pill-row" style="margin-top:14px">
              <span class="pill">Permanent</span><span class="pill">Full remote available</span><span class="pill">€40k to €75k</span>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="surface card card-prima">
            <div class="eyebrow">Why this asset</div>
            <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:850;line-height:1.15;">The vacancy already contains strong role specific information. The opportunity is therefore about hierarchy, not volume.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="shell">
          <div class="section-head">
            <div><div class="eyebrow">Before → What's wrong → After</div><h2>Move the distinctive proof up.</h2></div>
            <p>The strongest part of the opportunity is the ML Platform work. The redesign changes the order of information so the role answers the candidate's key questions earlier.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="asset-comparison">
            <article class="asset-panel">
              <div class="frame-title"><span class="chip chip-before">Before</span><span class="small">Current vacancy structure</span></div>
              <div class="vacancy-card vacancy-before">
                <div class="vacancy-brand">PRIMA CAREERS</div>
                <div class="vacancy-title">Senior Python Software Engineer</div>
                <div class="vacancy-meta">Milan · Permanent · Full remote · €40k–€75k</div>
                <div class="vacancy-copy">Are you looking for a new challenge? Fancy helping us shape the future of motor insurance?</div>
                <div class="vacancy-block"><b>Prima</b><span>Company story and wider context</span></div>
                <div class="vacancy-block"><b>Engineering</b><span>Wider Engineering context</span></div>
                <div class="vacancy-block muted-block"><b>ML Platform Domain</b><span>Distinctive role context appears further down</span></div>
                <div class="vacancy-block"><b>Role & requirements</b><span>Responsibilities, requirements and nice-to-haves</span></div>
                <div class="vacancy-block"><b>Why you'll love it here</b><span>Work Your Way · Grow with us · Thrive and perform</span></div>
                <div class="vacancy-cta muted-cta">Apply</div>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="asset-panel">
              <div class="frame-title"><span class="chip chip-after">After</span><span class="small">Redesigned mobile-first experience</span></div>
              <div class="vacancy-card vacancy-after">
                <div class="vacancy-brand">PRIMA CAREERS</div>
                <div class="vacancy-title">Senior Python Software Engineer</div>
                <div class="after-headline">Build the platforms that enable Machine Learning at scale at Prima.</div>
                <div class="vacancy-meta">Milan · Permanent · Full remote · €40k–€75k</div>
                <div class="vacancy-cta">Apply now</div>

                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">01 / Why this role exists</div>
                  <p>Join the ML Platform Domain and help build foundational platforms that support Machine Learning at scale, from experimentation to production.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">02 / Your impact</div>
                  <div class="mini-grid"><div><b>Scale</b><span>Shared capabilities for ML across Prima's markets.</span></div><div><b>Lifecycle</b><span>Experimentation, training, deployment and monitoring.</span></div><div><b>Collaboration</b><span>Product, Data Science, ML and Engineering.</span></div></div>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">03 / What you'll work on</div>
                  <div class="mini-grid"><div><b>Platform capabilities</b><span>Tools, shared services and infrastructure.</span></div><div><b>Complex engineering problems</b><span>Reliable, maintainable software and systems.</span></div><div><b>Technical guidance</b><span>Share expertise within the ML Platform Domain.</span></div></div>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">04 / Engineering environment</div>
                  <div class="phone-pills">{technologies.map(t => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
                  <p class="small" style="margin-top:8px">Additional technologies are relevant possibilities, not assumed day-to-day requirements.</p>
                  <div class="phone-pills" style="margin-top:6px">{optionalTechnologies.map(t => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">05 / Who you'll work with</div>
                  <p><strong>Product Managers</strong> · <strong>Data Scientists</strong> · <strong>ML Engineers</strong> · <strong>Software Engineers</strong></p>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">06 / How Prima supports your growth</div>
                  <div class="mini-grid"><div><b>Learning resources</b></div><div><b>Mentorship</b></div><div><b>Growth plan tailored to you</b></div></div>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section">
                  <div class="phone-label">07 / What to expect</div>
                  <p>Relevant hiring information is linked from the vacancy without duplicating the full company-wide process.</p>
                  <a class="text-link" href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">See the hiring process ↗</a>
                </div>
                <div class="after-section soft-end">
                  <div class="phone-label">08 / Why Prima</div>
                  <p><strong>Work Your Way</strong> · Grow with us · Thrive and perform</p>
                </div>
                <div class="vacancy-final"><b>Ready to build what's next?</b><a href="https://www.helloprima.com/careers/jobs/senior-python-software-engineer-77dc9214-4ed8-470e-93b0-4de8bbb1ccc4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apply now ↗</a></div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="shell grid two">
          <article class="surface card card-prima">
            <div class="eyebrow">What's wrong</div>
            <h3 style="margin-top:10px">The role is highly specific, but the most relevant proof comes too late.</h3>
            <p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">This is an information hierarchy problem, not an information volume problem.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="surface card">
            <div class="eyebrow">Design principle</div>
            <h3 style="margin-top:10px">Role → Impact → Work → Team → Technology → Growth → Hiring → EVP</h3>
            <p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">The mobile experience should answer the candidate's most important questions before asking them to work through broader company context.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="shell footer-grid">
        <div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Task 2</div><p style="margin-top:8px">Make something better</p></div>
        <a class="small" href="/prima-employer-brand-takehome/sources/">Sources & method →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
